# Everyone who holds copyright in this repository.
#
# Why this file exists: `docs/specs/2026-09-14-disclosure-authorship-and-citation.md`
# names an explicit contributor record as one of three things that make
# authorship "unambiguous and permanent," and notes it "becomes load-bearing
# the moment there is more than one contributor." Today there is one. Writing
# it down now costs nothing and means the record was never reconstructed from
# a commit log afterwards.
#
# This is NOT the list of who may skip the CLA sign-off. That is
# `.github/cla-exempt.txt`, and it is deliberately a different file answering
# a different question: this one records who owns copyright, that one records
# who does not need to sign an agreement with themselves. An automation
# identity belongs in that file and must never appear in this one — a bot
# holds no copyright.
#
# Outside contributors are added here when their first contribution merges,
# which by IP-POLICY.md rule 3 cannot happen before they have agreed to
# CLA.md.

Aleksa Zdravković <aleksazdravkovic@proton.me>  https://orcid.org/0009-0004-1535-1839
